}

\section{Multiple networks}{
Add \code{(1 | g)} to the formula, where \code{g} is the \code{netis_data} object's own
group column name, to fit a random intercept per network via \code{lme4}. A
\code{netis_data} object with more than one group and \emph{no} \code{(1 | g)} term is
